---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { isPlaceholder, site } from "../config/site";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="Privacy notice for the contact form on Jonas Eicher’s practice site."
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="section-label">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This notice covers the contact form on this website and nothing else.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      {site.legal.name}, independent practice, {site.legal.city}, {
        site.legal.country
      }.
      {
        isPlaceholder(site.legal.email) ? (
          <span class="placeholder">
            A contact email will be added to the Impressum.
          </span>
        ) : (
          <a href={`mailto:${site.legal.email}`}>{site.legal.email}</a>
        )
      }
    </p>

    <h2>Contact form</h2>
    <p>
      If you send the form, the site transmits your name, work email,
      organization, area of interest, and message so the enquiry can be
      answered. The legal basis is steps toward a contract, or legitimate
      interest in responding to a professional enquiry, under Art. 6 (1) (b) and
      (f) GDPR.
    </p>
    <p>
      {
        site.formAccessKey
          ? "Submissions are sent to Web3Forms, which delivers them by email. This site does not store its own copy of the message."
          : "Delivery is not active. Until it is switched on, the form validates what you type in the browser and does not transmit it."
      }
      When delivery is active, Web3Forms acts as the processor for that transmission.
      Their privacy information is published at web3forms.com.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and cookies</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. The host may process connection data
      such as IP address and browser type in server logs as part of providing
      the site. This site does not set analytics cookies and does not load a
      tracking script.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention and your rights</h2>
    <p>
      An enquiry is kept only as long as needed to answer it and to handle any
      engagement that follows. You can request access, correction, deletion, or
      restriction, and you can object to processing based on legitimate
      interest. You can also lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority. In
      Bavaria that is the Bayerisches Landesamt für Datenschutzaufsicht.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
